---
import DemoShell from '../DemoShell.astro';
import Control from './Control.astro';
---

<DemoShell
  id="demo-butler-volmer"
  code="D1"
  title="Butler–Volmer explorer"
  poster="d1-butler-volmer.svg"
  alt="Plot of current density against overpotential from the Butler–Volmer equation, with the linear response region marked around zero overpotential"
  aspect="5/2"
  stack={true}
  caption="Interfacial current density j(η), computed live. Left: linear axes with the small-signal line. Right: the same curve on Tafel axes with its two asymptotes."
  presets={[
    { label: 'Sluggish electrode: j₀ = 10⁻⁶ A cm⁻²', state: { 'd1-j0': 1e-6 } },
    { label: 'Asymmetric barrier: α_a = 0.3', state: { 'd1-lock': 1, 'd1-aa': 0.3, 'd1-ac': 0.7 } },
    { label: 'Cold cell: 250 K steepens both branches', state: { 'd1-T': 250 } },
  ]}
>
  <fieldset class="panel" slot="panel" disabled>
    <legend>kinetics</legend>
    <div class="control-cols">
      <Control id="d1-j0" label="j₀ / A cm⁻²" min={1e-6} max={1e-1} value={1e-3} scale="log" />
      <Control id="d1-T" label="T / K" min={250} max={350} value={298} step={1} />
      <Control id="d1-aa" label="α_a" min={0.1} max={0.9} value={0.5} step={0.01} />
      <Control id="d1-ac" label="α_c" min={0.1} max={0.9} value={0.5} step={0.01} />
    </div>
    <div class="switch-row">
      <label><input type="checkbox" id="d1-lock" checked /> lock α_a + α_c = 1</label>
    </div>
    <div class="panel-readouts">
      <span>b_a <output id="d1-slope-a">—</output></span>
      <span>b_c <output id="d1-slope-c">—</output></span>
      <span>linear region <output id="d1-linear">—</output></span>
      <span>R_ct <output id="d1-rct">—</output></span>
    </div>
  </fieldset>
  <Fragment slot="notes">
    <p>
      The Butler–Volmer equation for a single-step reaction: an anodic and a cathodic exponential
      whose difference is the net current. Three things are assumed, and each fails somewhere real:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>one rate-determining step, so a single pair of transfer coefficients describes the whole curve;</li>
      <li>no mass-transport limit, so the current keeps rising with overpotential instead of saturating;</li>
      <li>a film-free interface, with no SEI or oxide in series.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      The dashed line on the left is the linearised response, good to 5% inside the marked band.
      The dashed lines on the right are the Tafel asymptotes, with slope 2.303 RT/αF per decade.
      R<sub>ct</sub> is the small-signal charge-transfer resistance RT/((α<sub>a</sub>+α<sub>c</sub>)F j₀),
      the same quantity the impedance demo calls R<sub>ct</sub>.
    </p>
  </Fragment>
</DemoShell>

<style is:global>
  @media (max-width: 700px) {
    #demo-butler-volmer .demo-stage {
      aspect-ratio: 3/4 !important;
    }
  }
</style>

<script>
  import { initWhenVisible } from './runtime';
  initWhenVisible('demo-butler-volmer', async (shell) => {
    const { init } = await import('./d1-butler-volmer');
    init(shell);
  });
</script>
